  "locator": "Feature / option: thinking spans, strips the delimiters from the visible answer, and surfaces the reasoning text in a dedicated field so clients can render it separately. Chat Completions returns reasoning as reasoning_content on the assistant message. The Responses API returns reasoning as a reasoning output item that precedes the message item. Reasoning detection relies on a response template , which tells the server where a thinking span starts and ends. The server looks for one in two places, in order. The tokenizer’s response_template attribute, if the model ships one. A built-in fallback matched on the model architecture, for tokenizers that don’t ship a template yet. Models with neither are served without response parsing. The raw decoded text is returned as content and no reasoning field is surfaced, even if the model emits <think>...</think> tags. Enable reasoning on the server Use --reasoning to control whether the chat template emits thinking tokens. Value Behavior auto (default) Defer to the chat template’s default. on Force thinking on by setting enable_thinking=True in the chat template kwargs. off Force thinking off by setting enable_thinking=False",
  "kind": "publisher-report",
  "sourceKind": "primary",
  "accessedOn": "2026-09-15",
